    "full_text": "# Proposed SQL lesson delivery and ordinary learner receiving contract\n\nPrepared by estate-c945953fdeb7/product_execution_next for root review and an independent receiver. This is a source-only proposal; no staging, original parser, installed entry or browser invocation has occurred for the SQL lesson. Root must freeze the effective contract and release the serialized Mac interval before execution.\n\n## Chronology and authority\n\nThe twelve-question offer was sealed before root saw the author key. Root independently froze questions-only authority 05ea62581b4a7b47be3b7a22d7497b332b3f1629 at 11:01:32 UTC. Author source/key were sealed at 10:59:36 UTC. The post-seal comparison found all questions, answer choices, twelve SELECTs and 29 expected rows/110 cells equal. Root's already completed one-database independent SQL run is receipt 6abcda183f9fcdc42649b240745e61e4828f891d, with closure fe3f1f7095ef4911ff6f344e764d11e30de28fde, full invocation 40054958e107405aab72b1acc362935dec2b1751 and review 69ab32336bbf7ab307c86482143171f0e90cb8bd. All are retained unchanged. Actual tested dialect/runtime is SQLite 3.50.4 through Mac Python 3.13.7; original intended Linux SQLite 3.53.1 remains unexecuted under runtime amendment 20fbb70a7191fba9167bffd02a8c44b52af85c5c. No SQL is repeated in this contract.\n\nThis learner contract is later than source, answers and independent SQL qualification. It is not represented as a blind subject-authority freeze. It freezes one new physical course adoption and notes handoff before that operation. New author staging/parser source may have been privately drafted before this contract; exact reviewed source and input must be pinned before execution.\n\n## User outcome and ownership\n\nA learner receives an original twelve-question SQL NULL membership/absence course, a plain executable SQL worksheet and a worked Markdown guide. They use the already received local RecallWeave entry to import this separate saved JSON, complete one ordinary session, write a policy reflection and keep the actual physical study-notes text. This task adds only:\n- courses/sql-null-membership.json\n- courses/sql-null-membership.md\n- courses/sql-null-membership.sql\n\nSource parent: ec07bf3989132130759e5c00c6cb02eef19709d3. Reservation: https://github.com/Jacob-Met/RecallWeave/issues/257. SQL foundations, other SQL lessons, the original learner/model, catalog, picker, combined-output and saved-writing routes keep their owners. No existing installation, launcher, app source, catalog or dependency is changed.\n\n## Exact delivered content and navigation\n\nExclusive new delivery root:\n /Users/me/Developer/recallweave-sql-null-membership-c945953fdeb7\n\nMirror the three repository-relative courses/ paths there and write a final DELIVERY.json identity record only after staging and the one original-parser admission. All four files are new owned files; the three course files use mode 0444. This is a plain file delivery, with no new installer, command registration, service or listener.\n\nDelivered JSON:\n f32b3b429b209de60b5494b6f23dc8f863af0f1f\n 15,690 B, SHA256 e5cba4607be7f2be5ce90df3203e2393b5e2a5dbc20d245d9bd5289b8b064b5c\n\nDelivered corrected guide:\n 33fe4dd16b9cf94b5e696b30c6f5d76bca6ff3cb\n 22,908 B, SHA256 875496547f8d4abb38a584ab3ec952bbcdc40eb7e68f39651397480702d699ad\n\nDelivered worksheet:\n b482e5fa668aba1f571ed15c42ba749386a4c9cc\n 5,092 B, SHA256 0f27f9c4e9e3f678e8935cc9499af14c79c1289fbd7afc1bda2168829b31e78e\n\nTotal maintained delivery bytes: 43,690. The guide's two approved portability substitutions are reversible under proof 540c943f0e1be99512f1ea1dc4f9eb07ea01a931; original sealed guide 4b37631dc9430ebac8b4d6ab94d11b6b1ef140c5 remains separate evidence. Questions, answers, SQL and worked results are unchanged. The guide points to exact-parent SQL foundations and issue #257, while its worksheet command resolves from the delivery root. No SQLite CLI binary execution is claimed.\n\n## P — Author staging and one unchanged parser admission\n\nAfter root review/freeze and a fresh native guard, the fileless Python staging program admits all input pins, existing installed-file identities and ordinary runtime pins; refuses an existing delivery target; exclusively writes the three exact files; invokes one short Node child from /tmp; then writes the final delivery identity record.\n\nThe child calls parseDeck exactly once on the actual new physical JSON. It imports the full unchanged original ESM src/deck.mjs, Git f0f8a4b234489c2388f427633f548d56c6ed4c03, 4,894 B, SHA256 621438c166ec4bfafd9d87c698a1d46cb1722f4fb92dcbb8d9f52fce682c338b, via a data URL with the same bytes and no export rewriting. This source has no relative import dependency. A read-only source comparison establishes that the installed demo contains these exact parser bodies with only their export keywords omitted by its original bundling; no browser source is regenerated.\n\nRequire actual parser child exit 0, empty stderr, twelve unique null-member-01 through null-member-12 identities, the four exact concepts, title \"SQL NULL: membership and absence\" and complete returned-field equality to the delivered JSON. This admits the new course under the existing structural contract; subject authority comes from root's separate frozen comparison and SQL receipt. Do not run a parser matrix, malformed-input campaign, SQL query or original course case.\n\nCapture complete physical delivery pins, native modes/mtime strings and actual child wait/reap plus enclosing process exit. Every original installed byte/mode/mtime and each selected runtime must be identical before and after staging. If a guard or step refuses, preserve the actual partial state and raw receipt without deleting or repairing it. Do not enter learner use without a complete accepted delivery record.\n\n## L1 — Actual retained entry and physical new-course intake\n\nRetained installation:\n /Users/me/Applications/RecallWeaveEditDistance-c9459